<title>CANADA: Head of Canadian task force on banking resigns.</title>
<headline>Head of Canadian task force on banking resigns.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of a task force advising the Canadian government on revamping rules on the banking industry has resigned, the Finance Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>Toronto lawyer James Baillie spearheaded the task force, expected to make recommendations to the government next year on foreign competition, mergers and holding companies in the financial services industry.</p>
<p>Bailey stepped down after a newspaper report that he was tied to Bank of Nova Scotia's proposed C$1.25 billion takeover of National Trustco Inc.</p>
